    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0639" n="511" xml:id="pg511"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 360.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Langston</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 28,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 350.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit, in connection with, the
                    Department’s previous instruction No. 324 of January 20 last, a copy of a letter
                    addressed to the President by Mr. C. M. Bran, at Paris, France, in regard to the
                    case of Mr. Alexander C. d’Almena, now held in prison as a witness by the
                    authorities at Port-au-Prince.</p>
                <p>I have explained to Mr. Brun the nature of the Department’s instruction to you
                    relative to this case, and observed that his communication would be forwarded to
                    you in connection therewith.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d360-a1.xml" xpointer="d360-a1"/>
            </div>
